WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.300
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский, Episode 36, for 8 June, 2026.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.220
I'm Olia.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.580
Today's lesson is going to be a fun one, po яхали.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.520
Our word of the day is яблока.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.740
Яблока, яблухка.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.160
It sounds like яб, plus блок.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.180
Picture a big red apple you can yap about.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.440
The example sentence is я люблю яблока.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.180
Я люблю яблухка.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.200
That means I love an apple.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.480
Repeat after me, яблока.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.900
Now let's build more food words.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.860
Our first new word is хлеб, хлеб, хлеб.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.700
It sounds like хлеб, хлеб your hands for fresh bread.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.780
The example is дай мне хлеб, дай мне хлеб.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.620
That means give me bread.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.980
Repeat after me, хлеб.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.300
Next comes молоко, молоко, му, локо.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.660
Think of moon plus la ko.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.900
That is the sound a cow makes.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.120
The example sentence is я пю молоко.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.960
Я пю молоко.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.060
That means I drink milk.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.040
Repeat after me, молоко.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.940
Now we have вкусный.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.880
Вкусный, вкусный от.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.780
Вкус sounds like taste.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.340
It literally means tasty.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.260
The example is это вкусный суп.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:18.660
Это вкусный суп.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.240
That means this is delicious soup.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.240
Repeat after me, вкусный.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.900
Our next word is soup, суп, суп.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.280
It is exactly the same as the English word soup and easy win.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.060
The example sentence is суп горячий, суп горячий.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.060
That means the soup is hot.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.540
Repeat after me, суп now try frooked.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.500
Frooked, it sounds almost identical to fruit.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.340
The example is я емфрукт.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:48.760
That means I eat fruit.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.600
Repeat after me, frooked.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.500
Next we learn оваш, оваш, оваш.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.000
Say it like all fresh for veggies.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.980
The example sentence is морковь это оваш.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.880
Маршковь это оваш.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.040
That means carrot is vegetable.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.940
Repeat after me, оваш.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.720
Now we have чай, чай, чай.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.040
It sounds like чай, the same word in many languages.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.520
The example is pay-chai, pay-chai.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.120
That means drink tea.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.000
Repeat after me, чай.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.100
Our last vocabulary word is сыр, сыр, сыр.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.020
Say it like sur cheese, pretend you are a knight.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.500
The example sentence is сыр вкусный, сыр вкусный.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.680
That means the cheese is delicious.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.740
Repeat after me, сыр.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.020
Now for a quick grammar bite.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.180
Russian adjective like вкусный, change slightly to match the noun.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.260
Вкусный суп works for the masculine word soup.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.720
Вкусный вода works for the feminine word water.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.180
Вкусный яблоко works for the neuter word apple.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.020
English does not change adjectives this way.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.600
Russian makes the sentence flow smoothly.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.640
Now you can describe your food with the right ending.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.160
Russian love chai and often drink it from a samavar.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:08.540
A samavar is a special metal urn that keeps the tea hot all day.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.420
It is a warm part of daily hospitality.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.020
For our practice challenge, draw your favorite fruit or vegetable.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.820
Say it's Russian name out loud three times.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.040
If you are making breakfast, name each item in Russian.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.400
Say яблоко хлеб чай.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.080
Try using the word вкусный to describe it.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.220
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.560
Want to know a secret about чай?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.140
Did you know that the Russian word чай

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.660
and the English word T are actually cousins

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.100
from the same ancient root?

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.180
This word started in China as chai.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.220
It traveled along the silk road through Persian

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.300
and Turkish traders.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:50.020
It reached Russia in the 17th century via Karavan roots.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.820
Be careful though, the Russian word magazine

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:55.080
sounds like magazine, but means shop.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.240
That is a classic false friend.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.720
Next time you see Pt, remember its cousin чай.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.360
They both come from the same Chinese root.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.840
That connection is your secret shortcut

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.120
to remembering it forever.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.180
Молодец.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.700
That means well done.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.900
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.500
Practice saying today's words out loud.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:16.720
Even just one.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.020
And you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:20.360
See you next time.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.480
Пока, that Russian for bye.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.400
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.360
Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
